                <pb facs="0168" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg83"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1595: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gonzales</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-10T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 10,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Press despatch from Havana printed in New York <hi rendition="#italic">Sun</hi>
                    today states that you have issued a statement to the effect that United States
                    Government would not supervise the coming elections in Cuba.</p>
                <pb facs="0169" n="84" xml:id="pg84"/>
                <p>In view of the fact that you asked instructions of the Department in this matter
                    which were issued in Department’s telegram of December 8, 1 p.m., I am reluctant
                    to believe that this press report is accurate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
